---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';

const meta = {
  title: 'Why We Don\'t Charge Per-User — StdOut',
  description: 'The per-user pricing model is a relic of enterprise sales, not infrastructure automation. StdOut charges flat-rate because AI-powered ops should scale with your infrastructure, not your headcount.',
  canonical: 'https://stdout.app/pricing-manifesto'
};
---

<Layout {meta}>
  <main class="manifesto">
    <header class="manifesto-hero">
      <h1>Why We Don't Charge <span class="strike">Per-User</span></h1>
      <p class="lede">The per-user pricing model is a relic of enterprise sales, not infrastructure automation. StdOut charges flat-rate because AI-powered ops should scale with your infrastructure, not your headcount.</p>
    </header>

    <section class="manifesto-body">
      <article class="manifesto-section">
        <h2>The Per-User Tax is a Sales Artifact, Not a Technical Constraint</h2>
        <p>Per-user pricing exists because SaaS companies need predictable revenue and enterprise sales teams need a line item that scales with organization size. It has nothing to do with the actual cost of running the software.</p>

        <p>For infrastructure monitoring, this creates a perverse incentive: <strong>the more people you have helping keep systems up, the more you pay.</strong></p>

        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>Example:</strong> A 3-person ops team managing 50 servers pays the same Rootly price as a 3-person team managing 500 servers — but add one intern to help during incident response, and suddenly your bill jumps 25%.</p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="manifesto-section">
        <h2>AI-Powered Ops Eliminates the "User" Variable</h2>
        <p>StdOut's Observatory AI handles detection, diagnosis, and remediation autonomously. The number of humans reviewing incidents is irrelevant to the cost of running the system.</p>

        <ul class="benefit-list">
          <li><strong>Detection runs on a schedule</strong> — Watcher scans your stack every 5 minutes whether 1 person or 10 people are logged in</li>
          <li><strong>AI inference cost is fixed</strong> — Llama 3.2 and Qwen 2.5 run locally; no per-query pricing</li>
          <li><strong>Storage scales with infrastructure, not users</strong> — Your incident history grows with server count, not team size</li>
          <li><strong>Auto-remediation doesn't care who's watching</strong> — Automated fixes execute regardless of who's subscribed to alerts</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Charging per-user for this would be like charging per-viewer for a security camera feed. The camera runs whether 1 person or 100 people are watching.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="manifesto-section">
        <h2>Flat-Rate Aligns Incentives</h2>
        <p>Per-user pricing creates friction:</p>
        <ul class="friction-list">
          <li>Teams ration access to stay under seat limits</li>
          <li>New hires wait for budget approval before getting monitoring access</li>
          <li>Contractors and consultants get locked out to avoid overage charges</li>
          <li>Junior engineers can't learn incident response because "we only have 5 seats"</li>
        </ul>

        <p>StdOut's flat-rate model means:</p>
        <ul class="benefit-list">
          <li><strong>No access rationing</strong> — Everyone on the ops team gets full access, always</li>
          <li><strong>No surprise bills</strong> — Hire 5 people mid-quarter? Your StdOut price stays the same</li>
          <li><strong>No vendor lock-in games</strong> — We can't hold your org size hostage during renewal negotiations</li>
          <li><strong>Junior engineers can learn</strong> — Read-only observers don't inflate your bill</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="manifesto-section">
        <h2>What You Actually Pay For</h2>
        <p>StdOut charges $149/year flat. That covers:</p>

        <table class="pricing-breakdown">
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Self-hosted infrastructure</td>
              <td class="cost">$0/mo</td>
              <td class="note">Runs on hardware you already own</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>AI inference (local Ollama)</td>
              <td class="cost">$0/mo</td>
              <td class="note">Llama 3.2 + Qwen 2.5, no cloud API costs</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>StdOut license + updates</td>
              <td class="cost">$12.42/mo</td>
              <td class="note">One-time annual payment, billed yearly</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="total-row">
              <td><strong>Total (unlimited users)</strong></td>
              <td class="cost"><strong>$12.42/mo</strong></td>
              <td class="note"><strong>$149/year, flat-rate</strong></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <p class="footnote">Compare: Rootly starts at $1,800/year for 3 users. StdOut is $149/year for <em>unlimited</em> users.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="manifesto-section">
        <h2>When Per-User Pricing Makes Sense</h2>
        <p>We're not saying per-user pricing is always wrong. It works when:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The software's cost genuinely scales with user count (e.g., email inboxes, CRM seats)</li>
          <li>Each user consumes distinct cloud resources (e.g., file storage, compute credits)</li>
          <li>Value delivered is proportional to active users (e.g., collaboration tools)</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Infrastructure monitoring is none of these.</strong> The servers you're monitoring don't care how many people are watching the dashboard.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="manifesto-section">
        <h2>The SMB Reality</h2>
        <p>Small ops teams (1-5 people) don't have the budget flexibility to absorb per-user pricing shocks. When you hire your second ops engineer, you shouldn't have to explain to finance why the monitoring tool now costs 2x more.</p>

        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>Real scenario:</strong> A 2-person DevOps team at a SaaS company was using Rootly at $100/user/month = $200/month. They hired a third engineer. Rootly bill jumped to $300/month. CFO asked "why did our monitoring costs increase 50%?" The answer: "We hired someone to help keep the site up." That's broken.</p>
        </div>

        <p>StdOut's flat-rate model means hiring more ops engineers <em>reduces</em> your per-person cost, not increases it. If you have 1 person, it's $149/year. If you have 5 people, it's still $149/year — effectively $29.80/person/year.</p>
      </article>

      <article class="manifesto-section">
        <h2>Open-Core Future</h2>
        <p>StdOut is moving toward an open-core model where the core monitoring + AI detection is free (Apache 2.0), and premium features (multi-tenant, SSO, compliance reporting) are paid add-ons — still <strong>not per-user.</strong></p>

        <p>We'll charge for capabilities that create real operational cost (e.g., managed cloud hosting, white-label customization), not for the number of people using the software.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <footer class="manifesto-footer">
      <h2>Try It Yourself</h2>
      <p>Download StdOut, deploy it on your infrastructure, and invite your entire ops team. No seat limits, no per-user upsells, no surprise bills.</p>
      <div class="cta-buttons">
        <a href="/download" class="btn-primary">Download StdOut</a>
        <a href="/docs/quick-start" class="btn-secondary">Quick Start Guide</a>
      </div>
      <p class="footnote">Questions? <a href="mailto:support@seayniclabs.com">support@seayniclabs.com</a></p>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .manifesto {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 40px 20px 80px;
    color: #F0F0F8;
    font-family: -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .manifesto-hero {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 60px;
    padding-bottom: 40px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #1F1F35;
  }

  .manifesto-hero h1 {
    font-size: 48px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: #FB923C;
  }

  .strike {
    text-decoration: line-through;
    color: #EF4444;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  .lede {
    font-size: 20px;
    color: #C0C0D8;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .manifesto-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 60px;
  }

  .manifesto-section h2 {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #F0F0F8;
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    padding-bottom: 10px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #2A2A40;
  }

  .manifesto-section p {
    margin: 0 0 20px;
    color: #C0C0D8;
  }

  .callout {
    background: #0E0E18;
    border-left: 4px solid #FB923C;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    margin: 30px 0;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  .callout p {
    margin: 0;
    color: #F0F0F8;
  }

  .benefit-list,
  .friction-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 20px 0;
  }

  .benefit-list li,
  .friction-list li {
    padding: 12px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #1F1F35;
    color: #C0C0D8;
  }

  .benefit-list li:last-child,
  .friction-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .benefit-list strong {
    color: #22C55E;
  }

  .friction-list {
    color: #EF4444;
  }

  .pricing-breakdown {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin: 30px 0;
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .pricing-breakdown td {
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #1F1F35;
  }

  .pricing-breakdown .cost {
    text-align: right;
    font-family: monospace;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #FB923C;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .pricing-breakdown .note {
    color: #9090A8;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .total-row td {
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 2px solid #2A2A40;
    border-bottom: none;
    font-size: 16px;
  }

  .footnote {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #9090A8;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .manifesto-footer {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 80px;
    padding: 40px 0;
    border-top: 2px solid #1F1F35;
  }

  .manifesto-footer h2 {
    font-size: 32px;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    color: #F0F0F8;
  }

  .manifesto-footer > p {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: #C0C0D8;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }

  .cta-buttons {
    display: flex;
    gap: 16px;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .btn-primary,
  .btn-secondary {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 14px 32px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .btn-primary {
    background: #C2410C;
    color: #fff;
  }

  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: #EA580C;
  }

  .btn-secondary {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid #FB923C;
    color: #FB923C;
  }

  .btn-secondary:hover {
    background: #FB923C;
    color: #07070C;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .manifesto {
      padding: 20px 16px 60px;
    }

    .manifesto-hero h1 {
      font-size: 32px;
    }

    .lede {
      font-size: 16px;
    }

    .manifesto-section h2 {
      font-size: 22px;
    }

    .pricing-breakdown {
      font-size: 13px;
    }

    .pricing-breakdown .note {
      font-size: 11px;
    }

    .cta-buttons {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
    }
  }
</style>
